findings.suggestion:
Restore the original, broader check that covers all `AbstractBaseUser` subclasses and models related to the auth user model through inheritance:

```python
from django.contrib.auth.base_user import AbstractBaseUser

if field.name == "password" and (
    issubclass(field.model, AbstractBaseUser)
    or issubclass(get_user_model(), field.model)
):
    return render_password_as_hash(value)
```

Also restore the deleted test cases and test models to maintain regression coverage for CVE-2026-113733. If this revert is intentional (e.g., the CVE was rescinded), the release-notes removal should be accompanied by a clear justification; otherwise this change must not be merged as it re-exposes a known credential-disclosure vulnerability.
